      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since `prepareToClose` is called on a binder thread, `mCurrentRoute` is shared with the worker thread and thus access to it must be serialized. I see a couple of possibilities to fix this:\n\n 1. Instead of using `mCurrentRoute` here, fetch the route from `sSubmixRoutes` using `mPortId`. This will use already existing mutexes.\n \n 2. Add a lock for accessing `mCurrentRoute`. I think, this is less favorable approach as it will add locking to all worker paths, including `transfer`—we should really avoid that.\n \n 3. Instead of using a mutex we can use `std::atomic` for shared_ptr: http://go/cppref/cpp/memory/shared_ptr/atomic2. However, formally it\u0027s in C++20, I\u0027m not sure this will compile w/o project changes.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 310,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 310,
        "endChar": 53
      },
